From: REG-Linux <noreply@reg-linux.org>
Date: Sat, 2 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: skip VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation when not installed

VULKAN_DEBUG builds (auto-enabled by --enable-debug + HAVE_VULKAN in
qb/config.libs.sh) unconditionally request VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation.
Without the ~150 MB validation-layers package installed, instance
creation fails with VK_ERROR_LAYER_NOT_PRESENT (-6) and Vulkan is
unusable on DEBUG_BUILD=y images.

Two fixes:

1. vulkan_context_create_instance_wrapper(): enumerate available
   instance layers first; only add the validation layer (and its
   VK_EXT_debug_utils companion) when present.

2. vulkan_context_init(): the debug-utils messenger setup is guarded
   only by `vk->context.instance`. With VK_EXT_debug_utils not enabled,
   vkGetInstanceProcAddr returns NULL for vkCreateDebugUtilsMessengerEXT
   and the call segfaults. Also gate on the fn pointer.

After the patch:
  DEBUG_BUILD=y + layers installed -> unchanged.
  DEBUG_BUILD=y + no layers        -> RARCH_WARN, no debug messenger.
  DEBUG_BUILD=n                    -> unchanged (VULKAN_DEBUG undefined).

Reproduces on ODROID C5 (libmali r44p0-wayland-drm-g310-dmaheap):
SIGSEGV at vulkan_common.c:2582 because the fn pointer is NULL.

---
 gfx/common/vulkan_common.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/gfx/common/vulkan_common.c
+++ b/gfx/common/vulkan_common.c
@@ -915,14 +915,31 @@
          break;
    }

-#ifdef VULKAN_DEBUG
-   instance_layers[info.enabledLayerCount++]         = "VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation";
-   required_extensions[required_extension_count++] = "VK_EXT_debug_utils";
-#endif
-
    layer_count = ARRAY_SIZE(properties);
    vkEnumerateInstanceLayerProperties(&layer_count, properties);

+#ifdef VULKAN_DEBUG
+   {
+      uint32_t j;
+      int have_validation = 0;
+      for (j = 0; j < layer_count; j++)
+      {
+         if (string_is_equal(properties[j].layerName, "VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation"))
+         {
+            have_validation = 1;
+            break;
+         }
+      }
+      if (have_validation)
+      {
+         instance_layers[info.enabledLayerCount++]       = "VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation";
+         required_extensions[required_extension_count++] = "VK_EXT_debug_utils";
+      }
+      else
+         RARCH_WARN("[Vulkan] VULKAN_DEBUG build, but VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation is not installed; skipping.\n");
+   }
+#endif
+
    if (!(vulkan_find_instance_extensions(
             instance_extensions, &info.enabledExtensionCount,
             required_extensions, required_extension_count,
@@ -2561,11 +2578,12 @@
          | VK_DEBUG_UTILS_MESSAGE_TYPE_PERFORMANCE_BIT_EXT;
       info.pfnUserCallback = vulkan_debug_cb;

-      if (vk->context.instance)
+      if (vk->context.instance && vkCreateDebugUtilsMessengerEXT)
          vkCreateDebugUtilsMessengerEXT(vk->context.instance, &info, NULL,
                &vk->context.debug_callback);
    }
-   RARCH_LOG("[Vulkan] Enabling Vulkan debug layers.\n");
+   if (vk->context.debug_callback)
+      RARCH_LOG("[Vulkan] Enabling Vulkan debug layers.\n");
 #endif

    if (!vulkan_load_instance_symbols(vk))
